# Project Instructions

## Technology Stack
- .NET 8
- C#
- ASP.NET Core Web API
- SQL Server
- Azure Service Bus

## Coding Standards
- Follow SOLID principles.
- Use dependency injection.
- Use async/await for I/O operations.
- Use CancellationToken where appropriate.
- Avoid business logic inside controllers.
- Use constructor injection.
- Use structured logging.

## Architecture
- Follow layered architecture.
- Domain must not depend on Infrastructure.
- Application layer contains use cases.
- Infrastructure implements external dependencies.

## Testing
- Write unit tests for business logic.
- Write integration tests for APIs.
- Include failure scenarios.
- Validate idempotency.



Instructions tell Copilot how to behave.
Prompts tell Copilot what to do in a particular conversation.
Skills teach Copilot how to perform a particular task or workflow.
Agents define who performs the task and what responsibilities they have.
Tools allow an agent to interact with external systems or execute operations.	
